    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement by following the existing audit-logging pattern in `OwnerRestControllerV1`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger.\n2. **Enqueued the welcome notification on successful create** \u2014 in `addOwner`, right after the audit event is emitted and before the `201 CREATED` response is built, a new `enqueueWelcomeNotification(owner)` call emits a line via the `NOTIFY` logger containing both the owner id and the memberId:\n   ```\n   NOTIFY - welcome notification enqueued id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n   ```\n\nBecause it runs after `saveOwner` (which assigns the id) and after `assignMemberId`, both values are populated. It's also placed after all the rejection checks, so it only fires on a genuinely successful create.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a single line contains both the owner id and memberId \u2014 passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
